# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# IMPORTANT — why there is no blanket `* text=auto` rule here:
# DESCRIPTION, NAMESPACE and R/*.R were originally committed with CRLF line
# endings, while README.md, LICENSE and man/*.Rd are LF.  Adding a generic
# `* text=auto eol=lf` (or `*.R text eol=lf`) attribute would renormalise the
# 13 already-committed CRLF files, turning a one-line bug fix into an
# "every line changed" diff.  Those paths are therefore deliberately NOT
# listed below: they keep the exact bytes that are already in the repository.
#
# New / future files of the types listed here are forced to LF so that shell
# scripts, conda environments and Python sources behave identically on
# Windows, macOS and Linux.

# --------------------------------------------------------------- force LF
*.py            text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.Rbuildignore   text eol=lf

# ------------------------------------------- binary — never convert these
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.tif    binary
*.tiff   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.rds    binary
*.rda    binary
*.RData  binary
*.h5     binary
*.hdf5   binary
*.hic    binary
*.cool   binary
*.mcool  binary
*.bw     binary
*.bigwig binary
*.gz     binary
*.zip    binary
